{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"SB0020","billNumberShort":"S.B. 20","billNumberLong":"SB0020","fileNumber":"2026FL0497","shortTitle":"Natural Resources, Agriculture, and Environment Technical Changes","currentSubVersion":"0","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"STRATKJ","primeSponsorName":"Sen. Stratton, Keven J.","primeSponsorHouse":"S","floorSponsor":"ALBRECR","floorSponsorName":"Rep. Albrecht, Carl R.","floorSponsorHouse":"H","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses obsolete programs and makes other technical changes to statutes within the purview of natural resources, agriculture, and environment or related legislative committees.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>repeals language related to outdated authorizations to borrow or lend money from the Agricultural Water Optimization Account;<hr><ltbullet>repeals sections codifying the titles of a title, chapter, or part;<hr><ltbullet>requires certain annual reports to legislative committees be submitted by no later than October 1;<hr><ltbullet>repeals outdated reviews, reports, or studies;<hr><ltbullet>repeals outdated transitional language related to membership of boards;<hr><ltbullet>repeals outdated language regarding fees;<hr><ltbullet>corrects typographical errors;<hr><ltbullet>makes conforming amendments to sunset provisions;<hr><ltbullet>clarifies language regarding the federal Recreation and Public Purposes Act;<hr><ltbullet>repeals outdated deadlines for required management plans for water conveyance facilities;<hr><ltbullet>clarifies the procedure for the Great Salt Lake commissioner's submission of a strategic plan;<hr><ltbullet>repeals obsolete provisions related to mercury switch removal;<hr><ltbullet>repeals outdated provisions related to presenting rules for carbon capture and geological storage;<hr><ltbullet>repeals completed study of transportation, heating, and electricity-generating fuel storage reserves;<hr><ltbullet>repeals outdated provisions related to regulatory certainty;<hr><ltbullet>repeals outdated requirement to participate in a survey;<hr><ltbullet>repeals outdated emergency water resources chapter; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming amendments.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Patricia Owen","fiscalAnalyst":"Lacey K. Moore","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/26/2026","trackingID":"JADUWGRSNT","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2025-12-04 17:40:36.353","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2025-12-04 17:40:36.353","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LLFA","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ bill assigned to staff for fiscal analysis for SB0020","owner":"Legislative Fiscal Analyst","actionDate":"2025-12-04 17:40:41.950","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LFA1","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ bill sent to agencies for fiscal input for SB0020","owner":"Legislative Fiscal Agency","actionDate":"2025-12-04 17:40:41.950","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LFA2","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Senate/ received bill from Legislative Research","owner":"Waiting for Introduction in the Senate","actionDate":"2026-01-07 10:03:32.000","actionClass":"S","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"SRECLRGC","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ fiscal note sent to sponsor for SB0020","owner":"Version Sponsor","actionDate":"2026-01-13 17:05:22.130","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse"